    {
      "id": "showroom-connect-the-project-detail",
      "type": "face",
      "label": "CONNECT · Reading Page",
      "position": {
        "x": -90,
        "y": -670
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 450,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "showroom-connect-the-project",
          "nodeId": "showroom-connect-the-project-detail"
        },
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.detail",
          "scroll": "page"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;background:#f8fafc;color:#182943;font-family:Georgia,serif;padding:clamp(24px,5cqw,60px)\"><p style=\"font:900 12px system-ui;letter-spacing:.16em;color:#624aa0\">TWILITE / CONNECT / A REAL PROJECT</p><h1 style=\"font:500 clamp(36px,7cqw,65px)/1.04 Georgia,serif\">One project. Everything connected.</h1><p style=\"font:400 21px/1.5 Georgia,serif;color:#3a506b\">Look inside Twilite as a project, not simply a list of its documents. This guided example relates a goal, a plan, a design decision and an open question.</p><div style=\"background:#e8eef9;border-left:5px solid #6650a4;padding:18px 22px;font:500 15px/1.55 system-ui\">The project nodes below are a curated illustration. The linked Twilite project, product brainstorm, and release notes are actual separate graph documents. Connections shown here are authored relationships in this demonstration, not a claim that every linked graph is live-synchronized.</div><h2>Start with the goal</h2><p>Open Twilite to people who want to build with an AI, then keep and reuse the work. That goal introduces a plan, a product decision, and a question about the first experience.</p><h2>Follow the edges</h2><p>Goals are not isolated. A plan serves a goal; a decision shapes the plan; an open question can hold up the next step. The graph records those connections.</p><h2>Open another graph</h2><p>The portals below open the real Twilite project, its product brainstorm, and release notes. They aren't pasted copies. They are separate documents with their own identity and address.</p><div style=\"margin-top:26px;font:700 14px system-ui;color:#61419d\">Follow an idea → inspect the decision → open a real graph.</div></div>"
        }
      }
    },
